== REVIEW_QUESTIONS_2026-10-31
5:_reviews/REVIEW_QUESTIONS_2026-10-31.md:107: **G1 (item) — Q-6 judges its rival without Q-5 as recommended, so the rival is credited with numbers it cannot reach.** The instruction, section 3: «Where one answer depends on another, say so in one line, "depends on Q-<n>", and judge it with that answer as recommended; never assume another question's recommendation silently.» Q-5 declares the dependency in one direction: `QUESTIONS-PAPER.md:93` «Depends on Q-6 and Q-2.» Q-6 carries no "depends on" line. It judges Position A under Q-5 as recommended, `QUESTIONS-PAPER.md:113` «With Q-5 as recommended, 18, 17 and 17 children are on one list only», but grants Position B, `QUESTIONS-PAPER.md:115` «every child on the census: 60, 4 and 4», the row `QUESTIONS-PAPER.md:120` «| (c) 60, 8, 68 | yes | yes | both meet |». Under Q-5 as recommended, `QUESTIONS-PAPER.md:95`, the candidate list carries 3 + 2 = 5 of the 8 and the grant list 3 + 2 = 5, and 2 of the 8 are on the candidate and grant lists, off the census. Position B's 4 entries per list and "every child on the census" cannot both hold with that. `R/R_toy.log`: «Q-6 B (60, 4, 4) with Q-5 A as recommended: cannot be built: entries still needed per list after the 8 are laid [54, -1, -1]». The two positions of one table are judged under two different answers to Q-5. That is page item 2, «The judgements go in one table, position by test, so that a fact counted against one and not the other can be seen», and page item 5, «To contradict itself or the instruction». **What it carries into round 5:** the owner may rule Q-6 B and otherwise take the recommendations. The paper tells him B meets 60, 8 and 68, so nothing would warn him, and round 5 would receive settings no data can meet. Only Q-6 B with Q-5 B is buildable: `R/R_toy.log` «Q-6 A with Q-5 B … children 60 entries 68 … learners 64 caught 4» shows that Q-5's own rival holds under Q-6 as recommended. Q-6 is the only question with this fault. Each other rival was read with every other recommendation, and none is unbuildable without the paper saying so. Q-14's rival against Q-13's setting is flagged in both sections.
